# Tribal Knowledge (Index / Router) — {{PROJECT}}

Purpose: record major activities, issues, events, fixes, deployments, and operational decisions so
context survives a crashed session, a new context, or a future operator asking why work happened.
Entries are factual, dated, concise, and link to the stronger source document when one exists.

This file is a **map** to the per-quarter child files under `{{HISTORY_DIR}}/`. The history lives
in the children; nothing is ever pruned or edited there. {{HISTORY_NOTE}}.

How to use this file:

- Read this index during recovery or handoff, then grep the child for the quarter you care about.
- Prefer newer dated entries over older entries when they conflict.
- Use this file and the children as a map to source documents, not as a replacement for them.
- Add an entry **when the event happens** (not batched at session end) for: production deployment,
  incident, customer-impacting fix/refund/decision, major code change landing, monitoring/tooling/
  infra change, important operator decision. When unsure, record it.
- Every distinct `flush` adds one dated handoff entry on top of those (agent, task, changes,
  decisions with the actual WHY, evidence or commit — or "uncommitted" — dead ends, open questions,
  next action), even when nothing else changed. Never include secrets.

Where new entries go:

- **New entries go at the TOP of `## Entries` in the current child** (the newest file listed
  under Children). Append-only, newest first. `kb_tools.py append-history` places the flush entry
  there, opens the next quarter child on rollover, and starts a continuation child
  (`<quarter>-02.md`) when a child passes ~300 KB — listing each new child below.
- Do NOT edit, reorder or move existing entries in the children. Corrections are new entries.

Entry format (used in every child):

```text
Date:
Time:            (state the zone)
Area:
Event:
Impact:
Resolution:
GitHub ref:      (commit hash + branch; if uncommitted say so)
Source:          (link the stronger doc instead of duplicating)
Follow-up:
```

