## How to find an entry

Do not read a child top to bottom. Grep it, then read the block.

```bash
grep -n '^### {{DATE}}' {{HISTORY_DIR}}/<quarter>.md      # by date (entry headings start with the date)
grep -n 'F-12' {{HISTORY_DIR}}/<quarter>.md               # by finding ID
grep -n '<hash>' {{HISTORY_DIR}}/<quarter>.md             # by commit hash
grep -n '^### ' {{HISTORY_DIR}}/<quarter>.md | head -20   # the 20 newest entry headings
```

Then `sed -n '<start>,<end>p'` the block you need. Newer entries sit higher and win on conflict.

## Split rule

- A new quarter child opens on the first flush of the quarter and is listed above the current one.
- If a child exceeds ~300 KB mid-quarter, a continuation child (`<quarter>-02.md`) is started and
  listed here; entries are never moved out of the full child.
- Never edit, reorder, or move existing entries. Split, never delete.
